<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<manifest xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    xmlns:tools="http://schemas.android.com/tools">

    <!--
      AR is required in release, and optional everywhere else.

      Play filters an app declaring `android.hardware.camera.ar` as required off devices
      that cannot run it. That is the right trade for a shipped build: there is no non-AR
      drawing mode, so on an unsupported handset this app installs and can do nothing —
      which earns a one-star review rather than a user.

      The argument the other way, and why this override is scoped to release rather than
      moved into the main manifest:

      - It forecloses the non-AR fallback in PRODUCT_PLAN.md §7. If manual plan drawing
        ever lands, this has to come back out.
      - It costs the diagnostic signal. A user whose phone is unsupported cannot install,
        so they cannot tell us — and "which devices actually fail" is exactly what is not
        known yet.
      - Filtering is not perfect. Supported handsets do occasionally get filtered out by
        the feature check, and losing a real user is worse than an unusable install.

      Debug keeps `optional`, so a sideloaded build still installs on anything and still
      reports the truth through the device check. That keeps the diagnostic value where it
      is actually used — on test hardware — and spends the filter only where it protects
      someone.

      Note this does not remove any error handling. `com.google.ar.core` being *required*
      makes Play install ARCore alongside the app, but ARCore is a separate package that
      can still be missing, stale or refused, so CaptureActivity's failure paths stay
      exactly as load-bearing as they were.
    -->
    <uses-feature
        android:name="android.hardware.camera.ar"
        android:required="true"
        tools:replace="android:required" />

    <application>
        <meta-data
            android:name="com.google.ar.core"
            android:value="required"
            tools:replace="android:value" />
    </application>
</manifest>
